% ============================================================================
% farm-animal-product-processing.query — a worked recall over the
% agriculture farm-animal-product-processing library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "how is goat milk
% processed?": it states no agriculture fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine
% resolves each `?` against the `farm_animal_product_processing` rows and
% returns the processing method + the table's source/locator/trust. An
% animal/product pair the cited spans give no processing method for
% abstains honestly — the engine never invents one.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli farm-animal-product-processing.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "farm-animal-product-processing.adj"

? farm_animal_product_processing(goat, milk, $Processing)          % expect pasteurized
? farm_animal_product_processing($Animal, $Product, pasteurized)   % reverse bind — expect goat, milk
? farm_animal_product_processing(sheep, wool, $Processing)         % expect abstain — sheep's own cited span states no processing method for wool
